In para No.4 of the said decision, it was held as under;
"This Court is broadly in agreement with the submission made on behalf of the Petitioners that their lands cannot be touched by the State and the authorities, save by acquisition in accordance with law the Right to Property having been constitutionally guaranteed."
15. Refuting each and every contentions taken by the plaintiff, the learned standing counsel for the defendant has reiterated the contentions taken by the defendant in the written statement.
